kosha water-material

  -- H2O as a common-sense material — the everyday substance.
  -- bridges to: chemistry/water (molecular structure) + liquid (thermodynamic state).
  -- the same node from two perspectives: H2O is the chemistry, liquid is the phase.
  --
  -- everyday properties:
  --   liquid at 0-100°C (at 1 atm). solid below 0°C (ice). gas above 100°C (steam).
  --   transparent and colourless (thin layers). blue in bulk (selective absorption).
  --   refraction index 1.33 — bends light (apparent depth, rainbows).
  --   surface tension: 72 mN/m at 20°C. insects walk on it.
  --   high heat capacity: 4186 J/kg·K — resists temperature change.
  --   universal solvent: dissolves more substances than any other liquid.
  --   density maximum at 4°C — ice floats (unusual: most solids sink in liquid).
  --   coefficient of restitution: ~0 (liquid — no bounce, splashes).

